::PC_U05_L02_GP_Q01::
Question ID: PC_U05_L02_GP_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.PC.VC.10
Question:
In Vector Operations and Resultants, which response best shows mastery of MLA.PC.VC.10?
{
=A. Use addition, show the work, and explain the conclusion with evidence#Correct. This is the strongest response because it names the lesson concept, shows the reasoning, and connects the conclusion back to MLA.PC.VC.10.
~B. Start calculating before identifying the vector operations or the required feature#Incorrect. This is a misconception because calculation alone can answer the wrong question. First identify the vector operations and the feature being assessed. Review the lesson concept before trying a similar item.
~C. Use a related term from subtraction without checking whether it answers the question#Incorrect. This confuses related vocabulary with the actual target of the question. Use the lesson definition and check that the conclusion matches MLA.PC.VC.10. Review the lesson concept before trying a similar item.
~D. Give only a final answer without connecting the result to the lesson standard#Incorrect. This skips the explanation requirement. A mastery response must include reasoning so the Teacher of Record can see how the answer was found. Review the lesson concept before trying a similar item.
}
